B.a3a=A.a(s(["Izhar: pronounce the noon clearly before the throat letters \u0621 \u0647 \u0639 \u062d \u063a \u062e.","Idgham: merge it into the next letter when that letter is one of \u064a\u0631\u0645\u0644\u0648\u0646. There is a nasal sound with \u064a \u0646 \u0645 \u0648, and none with \u0644 and \u0631.","Iqlab: before the letter \u0628, the noon is turned into a hidden meem.","Ikhfa: before the other fifteen letters, hide the noon and keep a light nasal sound."]),t.s)
B.awr=new A.kd("Noon sakinah and tanween","\u0627\u0644\u0646\u0648\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0633\u0627\u0643\u0646\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0646\u0648\u064a\u0646","A noon with no vowel, or the tanween on a noun, is read in one of four ways. The next letter decides which.",B.a3a)
B.a13=A.a(s(["Do not rush past a shaddah on noon or meem.","The same nasal sound appears inside idgham, iqlab, and ikhfa."]),t.s)
B.aws=new A.kd("Ghunnah","\u0627\u0644\u063a\u0646\u0629","A nasal sound held for about two counts. You hear it most clearly when noon or meem carries a shaddah, as in \u0625\u0650\u0646\u064e\u0651 and \u062b\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651.",B.a13)
B.a3i=A.a(s(["The echo is stronger when you stop on the letter, as at the end of \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0641\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0642.","It is lighter when the letter is in the middle of a word."]),t.s)
B.awu=new A.kd("Qalqalah","\u0627\u0644\u0642\u0644\u0642\u0644\u0629","A light echo on five letters when they have no vowel: \u0642 \u0637 \u0628 \u062c \u062f. A common memory phrase is \u0642\u064f\u0637\u0652\u0628\u064f \u062c\u064e\u062f.",B.a3i)
B.a2i=A.a(s(["Natural madd: a vowel letter not followed by a hamzah or a sukoon. Hold it evenly, about two counts.","When a madd letter meets a hamzah, or you stop on a sukoon after it, the stretch is longer. A teacher sets the exact length used in your recitation."]),t.s)
B.awq=new A.kd("Madd, the stretch","\u0627\u0644\u0645\u062f","Alif, waw, and ya can stretch the sound. The natural madd is two counts. Longer madds are held beyond that.",B.a2i)
B.a2K=A.a(s(["Heavy: \u0642\u064e\u0627\u0644\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f, because the letter before has a fatha.","Light: \u0628\u0650\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650, because the letter before has a kasra."]),t.s)
B.awp=new A.kd("The lam in Allah","\u0644\u0627\u0645 \u0644\u0641\u0638 \u0627\u0644\u062c\u0644\u0627\u0644\u0629","The lam in Allah is heavy after a fatha or a damma, and light after a kasra.",B.a2K)
B.a2t=A.a(s(["Heavy: \u0631\u064e\u0628\u0650\u0651, \u0631\u064f\u0632\u0650\u0642\u064f\u0648\u0627.","Light: \u0631\u0650\u0632\u0652\u0642\u064b\u0627, \u0641\u0650\u0631\u0652\u0639\u064e\u0648\u0652\u0646."]),t.s)
B.awn=new A.kd("The letter ra","\u0627\u0644\u0631\u0627\u0621","The basic rule: ra is heavy with fatha or damma, and light with kasra. Stopping and a following ya create exceptions a teacher will show you.",B.a2t)
B.a24=A.a(s(["When you stop, the last letter is made still. A ta marbuta is pronounced ha.","Do not stop in a place that changes the meaning. If you do, go back and join the phrase."]),t.s)
B.awt=new A.kd("Where to stop","\u0627\u0644\u0648\u0642\u0641","Stop at the end of a complete phrase. Most printed mushafs mark a required stop, a stop you may take, and a place you should not stop.",B.a24)
B.a52=A.a(s(["\u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650 \u0645\u0650\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0634\u064e\u0651\u064a\u0652\u0637\u064e\u0627\u0646\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u064e\u0651\u062c\u0650\u064a\u0645\u0650","Then: \u0628\u0650\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u064e\u0651\u062d\u0652\u0645\u064e\u0670\u0646\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0631\u064e\u0651\u062d\u0650\u064a\u0645\u0650"]),t.s)
B.awo=new A.kd("Before you recite","\u0627\u0644\u0627\u0633\u062a\u0639\u0627\u0630\u0629 \u0648\u0627\u0644\u0628\u0633\u0645\u0644\u0629","Begin with the isti'adha, seeking refuge from Shaytan, then the basmala. At-Tawbah is the surah that is begun without the basmala.",B.a52)
